# Network Engineering Portfolio | CCNA 200-301

## Lab 06: VLANs, 802.1Q Trunking, Inter-VLAN Routing (ROAS), and Router DHCP Server

**Author:** Rafael Andrés Ramírez Benavides
**Role:** Junior Network Engineer


---

## 1. Executive Summary

This project demonstrates the design, deployment, and verification of a segmented Layer 2/Layer 3 corporate network architecture.

- The topology implements **Virtual Local Area Networks (VLANs)** to isolate broadcast domains between administrative and sales departments.
- **Inter-VLAN routing** is established using the Router-on-a-Stick (ROAS) pattern via 802.1Q subinterfaces on a Cisco router.
- **Cisco IOS DHCP Server pools** were configured per VLAN subinterface to automate dynamic IP address allocation across the infrastructure.

